Subject: [PATCH 17/91] Plutonium: the page alone sizes an embedded window

A parked window's maximize button (xdg_toplevel.set_maximized) went to
Ash, which resized the window to the work area while its element kept
its size: the window drew at one size in an element of another.

While parked, the client's maximize, minimize and restore requests are
answered with the state unchanged, and interactive moves and resizes
are refused. Whatever else changes a parked window's state or size
(Ash, aura-shell snap/float/PiP) is undone: it goes back to the normal
state at the page's size. A parked window's commits are no longer
clamped to the work area, and the page's size is forgotten when the
last element detaches.

